/ The preview pane renders the article with the public page's own helper and classes, so what
/ the editor shows is what the reader gets. It deliberately leaves out the site chrome —
/ breadcrumb, footer, related row — which is page furniture, not content.
/
/ It shows the last saved state, in the language the editor's tab is on; the editor reloads
/ this frame after every successful save and on every tab switch.
- locale = local_assigns.fetch(:locale, I18n.locale)
/ The locale marker goes on the article, not on the frame: Turbo replaces a frame's contents
/ and keeps the frame element's own attributes, so one up there would still name the language
/ the page was first rendered in.
= turbo_frame_tag dom_id(post, :preview), class: 'mg-preview__frame' do
  article.jn-post.mg-preview__article data-locale=locale
    h1.jn-post__title= post.title.presence || t('management.posts.editor.untitled')
    .jn-post__byline= journal_byline(post)

    - if post.photo.present?
      .jn-post__cover= image_tag post.photo.medium.url, alt: '', loading: 'lazy'

    .jn-body
      - if post.subtitle.present?
        p.jn-body__lede= post.subtitle
      = journal_body(post, locale)
